---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Dujiangyan vs Chengdu Panda Base - Which One to Visit?"
  description="Compare Dujiangyan Panda Base and Chengdu Research Base side by side: crowds, volunteer programs, ticket prices, transit, panda numbers, and our honest recommendation."
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-accent-600 uppercase mb-3">Compare</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-warm-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">
      Dujiangyan vs Chengdu Panda Base
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-warm-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      Two bases, two very different experiences. Here is everything you need to know to choose the right one for your Sichuan trip.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-warm-500">Last updated: July 2026</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick Comparison Table -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-5">Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-warm-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-warm-100">
            <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Feature</th>
            <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-medium text-accent-700 bg-accent-50/50">Dujiangyan</th>
            <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Chengdu</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-warm-200">
          <tr><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Crowds</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">Quiet, relaxed</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">Very busy, especially mornings</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Pandas</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">~20</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">~200</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Entrance Fee</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">CNY 58</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">CNY 55</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Volunteer Program</td><td class="px-5 py-3 bg-accent-50/50"><span class="font-medium text-accent-600">Yes</span> (CNY 700-900)</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">Not available</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Baby Pandas</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">Seasonal</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">Nursery area open year-round</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Transit from Chengdu</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">60 min via train + taxi</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">30 min via Metro Line 3</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Setting</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">Hillside, natural forest</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">Large manicured park</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Nearby UNESCO Sites</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">Dujiangyan Irrigation, Mount Qingcheng</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">None nearby</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Open Hours</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">8:30 AM - 5:00 PM</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">7:30 AM - 6:00 PM</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium text-warm-900">Best For</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600 bg-accent-50/50">Volunteers, couples, quiet visits</td><td class="px-5 py-3 text-warm-600">Families, first-time visitors, photographers</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Detailed Comparison -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 md:pb-24 space-y-12">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-4">The Experience</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
        Dujiangyan offers a quieter, more intimate panda encounter. With roughly 20 pandas spread across a hillside, you can spend unhurried time at each enclosure without pushing through crowds. The volunteer program — where you actually clean enclosures, prepare food, and hand-feed pandas — is the standout feature that Chengdu simply does not offer.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
        Chengdu, by contrast, is a much larger facility with around 200 pandas. It has the famous panda nursery where you can see tiny cubs (if you are lucky), extensive educational exhibits, and a more polished visitor experience. But it gets extremely crowded — arrive before 8 AM or expect long lines at popular enclosures. The <a href="https://www.panda.org.cn/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">Chengdu Research Base</a> is the flagship panda conservation center and worth visiting for its scale and variety alone.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-4">Which Should You Choose?</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mt-4">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-accent-200 bg-accent-50/30">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-accent-800 text-lg mb-2">Pick Dujiangyan if...</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-warm-700">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You want to do the volunteer program</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You prefer a quiet, uncrowded experience</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You are combining with the Dujiangyan Irrigation System or Mount Qingcheng</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You have a full day to spare for the trip from Chengdu</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You are traveling as a couple or small group</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-warm-200">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-warm-900 text-lg mb-2">Pick Chengdu if...</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-warm-700">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You want to see as many pandas as possible</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> Seeing baby pandas is a priority</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You are short on time (easy subway from downtown)</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> You are visiting with young children (no minimum age)</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-500 mt-0.5">+</span> This is your first panda experience in China</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-4">Can You Do Both?</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
        Absolutely — and many visitors do. A popular itinerary: spend a morning at Chengdu Research Base (arrive at opening), then take an afternoon high-speed train to Dujiangyan for a volunteer day the following morning. This gives you the full spectrum: the scale and nursery at Chengdu, then the hands-on, intimate experience at Dujiangyan. If you only have one panda day, our recommendation depends on what matters most to you: <strong>choose Dujiangyan for the volunteer experience, choose Chengdu for the spectacle.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
